OL,3,GNEWSAWhite-tailed eagle chicks fledge
OL,4,Afor fourth year
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhite-tailed eagle chicks have
OL,7,Fsuccessfully fledged from wild nests in
OL,8,FEngland for the fourth consecutive
OL,9,Fyear.
OL,11,FTwo out of five pairs of eagles
OL,12,Freleased by a reintroduction project
OL,13,Fsuccessfully bred and raised young with
OL,14,Fone chick fledging from a nest in
OL,15,FDorset and two more in Sussex.
OL,17,FThe project, run by Forestry England
OL,18,Fand the Roy Dennis Wildlife Foundation,
OL,19,Faims to return the species to England.
OL,20,FNine birds have been born in the wild
OL,21,Fsince it began in 2019.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
